invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: the Makefile stops refusing an AES value for a host object, so
  `make lib ROLE=server AES=extern` on an arm64 or x86-64 machine builds
  the host object, which holds the AES instructions, and drops the value
  without a word: the image's ch_aes_block, which the caller meant to
  run, never runs (docs/decisions.md 89). The lint's refusal rows build a
  server's host object under AES=soft and AES=extern and require make to
  stop.

--- old
ifneq ($(CPU_RUNTIME_DEF),)
ifneq ($(origin AES),file)
--- new
ifneq ($(CPU_RUNTIME_DEF),)
ifneq ($(origin AES),$(origin AES))
